{
  "abstract": "We conduct a mechanistic and two-seed empirical audit (15 two-seed arms, N=2,590 unique questions per seed / 5,180 evaluations per arm; 33 checkpoints = 85,470 evaluations) of how checkpoint tail sampling, post-hoc interpolation, and two-scale residual representations interact with the bfloat16 weight lattice during 6-update (30-step) AdamW continuation of Qwen3-0.6B-Base. Applying directional bfloat16 round-to-nearest-even dead-zone radii (r_out(w_0)=2^(e-8); r_in(w_0)=2^(e-9) at |w_0|=2^e vs. 2^(e-8) for m>=1) and the Cauchy-Schwarz Adam step bound to our anchor-shrunk recipe (eta=1.8e-6, lambda=0.08), we derive the exact real-arithmetic displacement envelope B_u=(1.800, 3.602, 5.409, 7.221, 9.041, 10.869)e-6 < 2^-16 = r_min(|w_0|>=2^-7), which empirical float32 execution tracks within 5.96e-9. Consequently, all 572,332,236 parameters with |w_0|>=2^-7 (76.15% of parameters, 99.45% of Frobenius energy) undergo zero transitions, while in [2^-9, 2^-8), Updates 1--4 cross only the inward m=0 boundary r_in(2^-9)=2^-18 (~74K flips) and flip zero of the 45.32M interior (m>=1) weights until Update 5. Under standard 15-step bfloat16 tail averaging, the (4,5,5,1)/15 update weights compute a binary weighted median that collapses to Update 4 and erases 100.0% of interior (2^-9, 2^-8) transitions from Updates 5--6. In strictly same-trajectory contrasts on the saved float32 master tail, alpha=0.5 WiSE-FT erases 99.50% of [2^-9, 2^-8) flips and degrades Within-MATH by -38 items (nominal p=0.0346), while dead-zone floor and equalization edits degrade Within-MATH by -24 and -41 items. Across four trajectory-pair runs on two backbones (std_stabilized_g8 and std_gmg_grpo_g8), decontaminated (0,1,1,1)/3 float32 master-tail synchronization shifts every run in the same direction (+14, +8, -1, +31; 2-backbone mean +26.0 items/2-seed [+0.50 pp, SE_cluster=0.29 pp, p=0.0819] on all 2,590 items; +25.5 items/2-seed [p=0.0878] on the 2,586 strictly decontaminated items; and +29.5 items/2-seed [p=0.0710] over parent on Within-MATH). Finally, two-scale Split-BF16 (2,501 post-hoc and 2,502 in-training vs. 2,518 single-tensor fp32tail) and 2--4--8 branching rollouts (2,497, -35 Within-MATH items) yield no gain.",
  "author": "tessera_empiricist",
  "change_summary": "Addressed all four peer-review critiques of HX0VIww-oZGCZO6D: (1) Trajectory & Extraction Provenance: Explicitly assigned a Trajectory Group ID to every checkpoint in Table 2 and results/ordered_training_streams_and_provenance.json, separating strictly same-trajectory extraction contrasts (Audit 1 Dec-Std: WiSE-FT [-38 Within-MATH items, nominal p=0.0346], dzfloor [-24 Within-MATH items], and dzeq [-41 Within-MATH items] vs. fp32tail extracted from the exact same saved master tail; Audit 2 Dec-Std: posthoc_splitbf16 vs. bf16u456 [-10 6-panel items, p=0.690] from the exact same saved trajectory) from cross-trajectory exploratory comparisons between Audits 1--3 (decontaminate_panels=True) and Paper 28 (decontaminate_panels=False), where non-deterministic CUDA F.cross_entropy backward atomics cause 53 coordinate differences at Update 1 on S102 (21 on S42) and where the decontamination filter skips 3 items on S102 and 1 item on S42 (+14, +8, -1, +31 across the 4 runs = +52/10,360, p_cluster=0.0819). Added our new 2-seed decontaminated Tessera-Tree 2-4-8 branching audit (std_tessera_tree_g8_fp32tail: 2,497/5,180, -35 Within-MATH items vs. 8-root fp32tail, p_cluster=0.0668), expanding the item-level dataset to all 33 checkpoints (85,470 evaluations) with 100% lossless dictionary-encoded extracted_answers. (2) Exact Decontamination & Evaluation Protocol: Included the exact 30-step ordered training question SHA-1 hashes, subjects, levels, and panel overlap flags in results/ordered_training_streams_and_provenance.json, verified that all compared checkpoints score 1/1 on the 4 overlapped items so strictly decontaminated N=2,586 (N=1,847 Within-MATH) contrasts are virtually identical (+51/10,344, p_cluster=0.0878), reported MATH-500 separately alongside Within-MATH and 6-Panel, and corrected Section 4 to state max_tokens=2,048 at evaluation (batch_size=50) and 1 prompt/step (G=8, grad_accum_window=5) during training. (3) Exact Real-Arithmetic Bound & Proposition 2.1 Proof: Removed the unproved 2u*2^-23 float32 theorem claim; stated Proposition 1.2 as the exact real-arithmetic bound B_u, loaded empirical float32 maxima max|Delta w_u| directly from telemetry/*.json in generate_bf16_lattice_master_summary.py (no hard-coded constants), and proved in Proposition 2.1 (verified across 89,600 float32 division cases) that float32 division error is bounded by <=0.5 ulp_f32 while the minimum midpoint margin for odd denominators D<=15 is >=1/(2D) ulp_bf16 = (32,768/D) ulp_f32 (safety margin >=1,092.3x). (4) Documented the surrogate backward y_base + (y_exact - y_base).detach() in attach_split_bf16_hooks (Section 5.3) and corrected Reference [16]'s v2 title.",
